WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.520
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:13.380
The reading from the Sinaxadion for June 21st, on which we commemorate the Holy Martyr

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:18.260
Julien of Celicia.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:24.700
On the 21st of the month, we celebrate the memory of the Holy Martyr Julien of Celicia.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:32.420
A native of Anzarbus in Celicia, Secunda, now Agasli, St. Julien was the son of a pagan

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:39.260
senator, but had received a solid Christian education from his devout mother, Asclipiolora,

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.420
and was greatly learned in the inspired scriptures.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:49.060
During Diocletian's persecution, he was denounced to the cruel governor, Marcian, who was

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:56.940
inflavious, and when he refused to sacrifice to idols, the governor had him flogged and threatened

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.460
him with terrible tortures.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:08.300
The saint replied, I am not afraid of the torments, and nothing will make me deny the

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:16.540
law that was given me in my childhood, even if you burn me in the fire of these torments.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:24.260
For I have Christ who strengthens me, and it is to him that I unceasingly offer a sacrifice

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.940
of praise.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:33.700
The perverse magistrate forced him to swallow food, sacrificed to idols, but the saint replied

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:40.020
that whatever is done under duress cannot be counted as a sacrifice.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:46.060
After having had him flogged again, Marcian took him to Anzarbus, the soldiers beating

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.420
him the whole way.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:55.060
Arriving in the town, the valiant martyr appeared before the tribunal, where he showed the

00:01:55.060 --> 00:02:01.980
same resolution, despite the wine offered in impious oblation that they forced him to drink,

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.140
and the incense that they put in his hands.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:14.300
He was then transferred to a guy on the Gulf of Issykos, famed for its temple of Asculepios,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:21.140
and was ordered to submit to the emperor's orders on pain of being consigned to the flames.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:27.060
Julian replied to the governor, and what is stopping you doing that?

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:33.140
They then summoned his mother, who had followed him, hoping that her entreaties would move him.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:40.420
Asculepiodora obtained permission to spend three days with her son in his prison, but instead

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:47.140
of exhorting him to save his life, she encouraged him to remain firm to death in the confession

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:52.780
of his faith in Christ, the conqueror of death.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:03:00.260
And she particularly said to him, you know what is of real benefit to you, because I taught

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:07.100
it to you, act then to give glory to the one true God.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:12.940
The time allowed having passed Marcian realizing that he had been tricked, ordered that Julian

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:19.420
be put in a sack filled with sand, and that snakes, scorpions, and all sorts of venomous

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:26.020
animals be put in it with him, and that he be cast into the sea.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:30.620
Although the valiant martyr's body was thus plunged into the depths, his soul flew off

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:36.700
to the highest heaven, to sit in the assembly of the first born.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:42.180
His relics were later found and translated to the vicinity of Antioch, three miles from

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:48.260
the city on the Daphne Road, where a chapel was built in his honor greatly venerated because

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:56.020
of the innumerable healings that took place there, especially of those possessed by demons.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:04:03.260
This chapel was burned down during the Persian invasion of 537.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:10.260
Through the prayers of our Holy Fathers, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
